window.docContents[210].resolve({"/Tier-3___-trusted___-not-read/AArch64-semantics/Arm64.Trusted.Syscalls.Fs.Stat/#file-Arm64___Trusted___Syscalls___Fs___Stat":{"contents":"Paper › arm64-semantics/Arm64/Trusted/Syscalls/Fs › Stat.leanTier 3 · arm64-semantics\n\nTier 3 · arm64-semantics used by the symbolic proof 2 headline theorems depend on it 37 of 65 lines trusted source ↗Trusted, reviewed with the engine. The AArch64 model in arm64-semantics is Tier 3: it is reviewed in its own repository (check-trust-guards). The declarations that the headline statements use are shown for completeness.\n\nLinux fstat SyscallModels AArch64 fstat (__NR_fstat = 80, Linux fs/stat.c newfstat) and the 128-byte little-endian struct stat layout (include/uapi/asm-generic/stat.h).\n\n\n\ndef SYS_FSTATL25–26 ↗#Linux AArch64 fstat syscall number (__NR_fstat = 80, include/uapi/asm-generic/unistd.h:229).\n\ndef encodeLinuxStatL28–41 ↗#Serialize a 128-byte little-endian Linux AArch64 struct stat (include/uapi/asm-generic/stat.h:24, fs/stat.c:405 cp_new_stat). Regular files report mode 0644 (0x81a4), st_nlink = 1, byte length st_size, and 512-byte sector count st_blocks; permission bits are metadata only and permission checks are not modeled. Directory entries synthesize fixed metadata (st_mode = 0x41ed for 0755, st_nlink = 2, st_size = 0, st_blocks = 0) independent of directory contents or filesystem.\n\ndef execFstatL43–63 ↗#Execute fstat(fd, statbuf) (__NR_fstat = 80, fs/stat.c:525 newfstat). Models .localFile and .localDir descriptors, raising .Exception on unmodeled .stdio or non-file descriptors. Validates fd before checking statbuf write permissions (EFAULT_RET), matching vfs_fstat followed by cp_new_stat.\n\n\n\n","context":"AlphaProof Code: Verifying Signal’s Security at the Machine-Code Level","header":"arm64-semantics/Arm64/Trusted/Syscalls/Fs/Stat.lean","id":"/Tier-3___-trusted___-not-read/AArch64-semantics/Arm64.Trusted.Syscalls.Fs.Stat/#file-Arm64___Trusted___Syscalls___Fs___Stat"}});